  "boundaries": [
    "Linux KVM on the recorded Intel P/E cores only. The API does not guess architecturally undefined successful arithmetic flags or infer a hardware profile from the host.",
    "The software read owner covers divisor memory faults before #DE and publishes both outputs only after quotient checks. There is no new memory RMW or write permission requirement.",
    "The full paging suite and existing scalar/fast-system owners were rerun. Two LA57 tests are unavailable on this host; no general i386 exporter, real/VM86, tasks/call gates, debug producers, software SMM/enclave/AEX/EPCM or complete CET/FRED event coverage is implied.",
    "No LLVM or NeverC compiler change is needed for this software executor. Native LLVM protected code16 DIV/IDIV is a separate reproduced gap. NeverC has no i386 frontend target. Global completion and the final SDK release/pin remain open."
  ],
